> Indonesia - Eko[ Nug]roho and "Wayang Bocor"
Eko Nurgoho is one of[ Indonesia]'s most provocative young artists whose style is a unique mix of[ Indonesia]'s rich[ traditions] and popular culture tinged with dark humor. Using a[ distinctive] blend of high and low art,[ Nug]roho' "Wayang Bocor" is a contemporary form of theater in which[ pupp]ets and actors[ weave] together traditional elements of[ Indonesian] 'wayag' ([shadow pupp]ets) with live theater and scripts that[ cast] a satiric view of[ contemporary] subjects. The show "God Bliss" tells the[ story] of how Islam came to Java, and became[ absorbed] as part of Javanese culture that includes elements of[ Hindu]ism, Buddhism, and[ anim]ism. Sim[ultane]ously playful and[ penetrating].

